## Why This Is Asked
This checks ability to design secure, compliant AI deployments across clouds, covering governance, identity, data integrity, and responder readiness.

## Key Concepts
- CISSP domains: Security & Risk Management, IAM, Security Architecture, Security Operations
- Policy-as-Code (OPA/Rego)
- Model provenance, artifact signing, immutable logs
- ABAC, least privilege, cross-cloud auditable logs
- Incident response for model poisoning and supply-chain risk

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: sign artifact (simplified)
const crypto = require('crypto');
function signArtifact(data, privKey) {
  const sign = crypto.createSign('SHA256');
  sign.update(data);
  sign.end();
  return sign.sign(privKey, 'hex');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you integrate policy checks into CI/CD and runtime gates?
- How would you validate provenance and detect poisoned models before serving?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical CISSP concepts for edge-to-cloud security in a high-velocity fleet context, including hardware-backed identity, secure update, provenance, and incident response.

## Key Concepts

- Edge attestation with TPM/TEE
- Ephemeral credentials and mTLS
- SBOM and reproducible builds (Sigstore/SLSA)
- Runtime integrity and OTA security
- Incident response, tabletop exercises, and tooling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify firmware signature on boot
function verifyFirmware(signature, payload) {
  const isValid = verifySignature(payload, signature);
  if (!isValid) throw new Error('Invalid firmware');
  bootMeetsIntegrityChecks();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale attestation verification across 200k devices?
- What tooling would you use for SBOM generation and artifact signing at the edge?
